course: dictionary
lesson: 1411
title: One word, two jobs: career
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job in a sentence, and the words around them show which job they are doing. Career is one of these words. It can be a noun, which is a thing or a person, or a verb, which is an action.
explain: As a noun, a career is the work someone does for a long part of their life. «Taking a career break» means not working for a while, often because there is no job. Your career at school is simply the time you spend there.
explain: As a verb, to career means to move fast and out of control. «The bike careered down the hill» means it rushed, not that it was steered carefully. To check your meaning, swap in a word like rushed and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A career is the job or kind of work someone does for a long part of their life.
fact: «Choosing a job» means thinking about what you enjoy, what you are good at and what pays enough.
fact: A salary is yearly pay, and an hourly rate is pay for each hour worked.
fact: Most professional footballers retire in their 30s, so many of them need a second career.
fact: Many adults change jobs or careers more than once.
exercise: «Taking a career break» means what? | Getting a new bike | Running a race very fast | Starting a brand new school | *Not working for a while
exercise: «The bike careered down the hill.» What does careered mean? | *Moved fast and out of control | Stopped at the top of the hill | Climbed up slowly | Was painted bright red
exercise: What is a salary? | *Yearly pay | A job you do for your whole life | Pay for each hour worked | A kind of school trip
test: In «your career at school», what does career mean? | A kind of bell | A school trip to the museum | A pile of books | *The time you spend there
test: Why might a professional footballer need a second career? | Because football is always boring | *Because most retire in their 30s | Because they are too tall for the team | Because they hate playing football
exam: Which sentence uses career as a verb? | *«The cart careered down the steep hill.» | «She chose a career in nursing.» | «Taking a career break is allowed.» | «Her career at school was happy.»
